<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Crown Demands but the Heart Desires</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;"Tao, she isn't dead. I would know if she died, I would feel it in my bones. She is out there somewhereâ€”even if- if we canâ€™t find her." She could feel tears on her cheeks. If she were in front of anyone but Tao, she would be mortified.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"My liege, it's been well over two years. We searched all Etheria and there has not been a single sighting of Queen Adora. You need to let her go." He breached protocol and pulled Catra into a tight hug.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œYour people wish to see you happy, Catra." Tao murmured as he wrapped his tail around her waist, holding her close. Catra smiled at Tao, a sad thing that didn't reach her eyes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;"I'm not sure that is in the cards for me anymore Tao. Right now, we need to focus on defeating the Horde and bringing peace to Etheria. Happiness will have to wait."&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;OR&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Queen Adora is long presumed dead. King Catra's only viable political option to defeat the Horde makes her stomach roll: a marriage uniting Halfmoon with Bright Moon. When King Catra's decision coincides with the appearance of the legendary warrior She-ra, the choice becomes harder than ever. Medieval/Political Warfare AU.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>ResFlower</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
